KZ3 patch 2166 (RSX pass 154): the pipeline template finder sees fragment programs at 8 mod 16.
Fragment programs at 8 mod 16 were missed: rsx_pt_scan probed
only addresses that are 0 mod 16, so a fragment program at 8 mod 16 (in the EBOOT's
writable data segment) was invisible until the game copied it 16-aligned elsewhere.
- runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp: ppu_image_ranges(out, max) exports the loaded PT_LOAD ranges (generic, no behaviour change).
- libs/video/rsx_pso_template.h: rsx_pt_scan_step(base, len, t, hit, user, step, kind_mask) with RSX_PT_KIND_VP/FP; rsx_pt_scan
  is step 16, both kinds (unchanged).
- libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c: rsx_live_draw_set_image_ranges(pairs, n) (up to 8; ld_pt_start pulls the loader's through a weak
  ppu_image_ranges when nobody set them); the scout runs ONE step-8 pass over the committed parts of those ranges on its first
  scan after the guest base resolves, queues what it completed, and runs the general (step 16) pass only while records are still
  unqueued. Zero ranges = the old scout. Diagnostic: hits counted by guest address mod 16 (0/4/8/12), per kind, image pass vs
  general pass, printed after the scan lines as "[pso-template] found by guest address mod 16 (image pass/general pass): ...";
  the image pass has its own line. The general step is NOT changed (K4 evidence decides whether FPs need step 8 there).
Host test: tools/smoke/test_pso_template.sh.

